## Context

PR #157 was squash-merged into `main` as `f5b3a97288e043b1cb7263fa40093450111a1a38`.

The read-only real observation profile has now been exercised on the Jetson with the installed legacy stack retaining all authorities. The following physical inputs are available without Salus owning hardware:

- `/salus/imu/data`: selected Pixhawk IMU, hardware-validated read-only (~10 Hz, observed frame `base_link`);
- `/wheel/odometry`: existing legacy Ackermann odometry (~10 Hz), currently consumed by the authoritative legacy local EKF;
- `/odometry/local`: authoritative legacy local EKF output;
- legacy TF remains the sole authority for `odom -> base_footprint`.

The next migration cut must validate Salus local sensor fusion while preserving those authorities.

## Decision

Implement **local localization only**, in shadow.

Do not start global localization yet.

Architecture:

```text
legacy MAVROS /imu/data
  -> existing real_observation Pixhawk adapter/selector
  -> /salus/imu/data
                         \
                          -> Salus local EKF shadow
legacy /wheel/odometry  /       |
                                 -> /salus/localization_shadow/odometry/local

legacy local EKF remains:
  /wheel/odometry + /imu/data
    -> /odometry/local
    -> authoritative odom -> base_footprint TF
```

The shadow EKF publishes odometry only. It must never publish TF.

## Why not canonical wheel odometry yet

Do **not** insert `kinematic_conversion` or `kinematic_ackermann_odometry` into this physical cut.

The current physical `DriveTelemetry -> TractionMeasurement/SteeringMeasurement` wire path is validated, but real mechanical calibration is explicitly still pending:

- Hall-derived motor/transmission speed is not ground speed;
- AS5600 linkage angle is not yet a validated virtual-center wheel angle;
- direction/sign still contains inferred information.

