**Conclusion: a duplicate of #3848.** The bit-stream cast this issue named is not at fault.

The probe was:

```systemverilog
a[3].isfloat = 1; a[3].n.i = 3;
tb = tagbits'(a[3]);
a[4] = tagged_st'(tb);
```

with `tagged_st a [7:0]`, a struct holding a bit and an unpacked union of int and shortreal. It read `t=0 v=0` because the member writes to the element `a[3]` are never stored. `a[3].isfloat` reads 0 straight after the write, with no cast involved, and so does `xa[1].i` of a plain `struct { bit f; int i; } xa [3:0]`. That is #3848: a write to an element of a module-level unpacked array of structs is not stored.

Cast on a struct variable rather than an array element, `tb = tagbits'(z); w = tagged_st'(tb);` round-trips (`1 3`), as IEEE 1800-2023 §6.24.1 asks. So does `33'(za[2])` of an element assigned whole, `za[2] = z`.

